{% extends "verify_claim/v21.j2" %}
{% block weight_quote_schema %}, "weight_quotes": {}{% endblock %}
{% block weight_quote_instructions %}
For each record, add short verbatim fragments from the supplied abstract under "weight_quotes". Use these keys when the text supports them:
- design: the actual study type, allocation, or experimental system;
- precision: the sample for this result (reuse n_quote when present);
- effect: the size or direction of the same result, including a null result when reported;
- comparison: the actual comparison (for example the intervention and control groups);
- context: the intervention, population, species, or other condition that explains the relevant match or mismatch.
When the main quote contains the evidence, copy only the relevant wording from it. Otherwise copy a contiguous fragment from elsewhere in the same abstract. Omit a key when the supplied abstract does not substantiate it. Keep the original fields and their extraction rules. Do not infer missing data or assign weights.
{% endblock %}
